                "quoted_status_profile_username": "USATODAY",
                "reply_count": 479,
                "retweet_count": 685,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "They could be explaining to millions of Americans how their horrible budget will gut Medicaid and cost lives.\n\u2028They could be voting to release the Epstein files.\n\u2028They could be fixing their broken immigration policies.\n\u2028They could be addressing the rising costs that are crushing families.\n\nBut instead, House Republicans are busy naming an opera house after Melania Trump.\n\nWhat, exactly, has she contributed to the arts that makes this a national priority?",
